  "descriptionMd": "The array `prices` lists a stock's price on consecutive days: `prices[i]` is the price on day `i`.\n\nYou may make **at most one trade**: buy one share on some day and sell it on a **later** day. Return the largest profit you can lock in. If every possible trade loses money (or breaks even), don't trade and return `0`.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nprices = [8, 2, 6, 1, 4, 9]\n→ 8\n```\nBuy at 1 on day 3, sell at 9 on day 5.\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nprices = [9, 7, 4, 3]\n→ 0\n```\nThe price only falls, so no trade is profitable.",
  "constraints": ["1 ≤ prices.length ≤ 10⁵", "0 ≤ prices[i] ≤ 10⁴"],
